Z||000012||fieroX||12-22-2001||02:51 AM||||Thats why I wont let anyone touch my car, I do everything myself.  And I cant wait until the day I run into this clown running around here in a 1994 RT/10, this guy thinks this piece runs low 12's because it has an exhaust that adds 50 hp.  Im going to teach him a lesson in supercharged V6, and taillights.<P>------------------<BR>    <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroX.com" TARGET=_blank>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fierox.com/logo2small.gif">  </A><BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroX.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroX.com</A><BR>coming soon L67 powered 87 coupe||||reg||1
Z||000013||turbo86se||12-22-2001||11:13 AM||||The LAST time I went to a pull-up oil change place (Havolinne), I handed over the keys to my turbo-charged 86SE to the man working, he pulled my Fiero around back with the front of the car over the pit. For a minute or two the guys couldn't figure out how to open the hood, I came out, asked for my keys back. The guys said, "how do you get your hood open?" I asked again for my keys back. They said,"why?" Still very calm, I said, "the engine's in the back!" Now the guy is starting to get defensive, he says, "are calling us idiots?" I said, "no, there's just no way I'm going to let you work on my car if you don't even know the engine is in the back, it's a special car!" Then he's like "it's only a Pontiac!" I said, "well, you got something right!" I hopped in my SE and hauled out of there!<P>I had to get my oil-changed, was leaving for Williamsburg the next day. Went down to the other Havolinne that was too busy in the first place, been there many times, very cool people. Pulled right up, told the manager about what happened at the other store, he apologized, and they were very good to my baby. You should have seen them cleaning my oil pan! LOL  <P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/SC.jpg"> ||||reg||13
Z||000014||rogergarrison||12-22-2001||08:03 PM||||A quick rehash of an old story I had. Took my car to Dave Gill Pontiac here in columbus to get the e brake and exhaust recall done for free. The car ran perfectly except for manifold crack and no ebrake. In fact just got back a few hours before I dropped it off from a long roadtrip. Went to pick it up, ebrake worked, no exhaust leak. They broke the clutch yoke, burned out the clutch disk, pinched off 2 plug wires, a couple of hoses and a few other assorted wires. I knew the second I got in it something was wrong, could barely get it going,couldnt get it over 45 mph on freeway, no heat. called them soon as I pulled into garage. Sent it back to them on a wrecker. They said my heat didnt work because i had the wrong thermostat 160*, so threw it away and put in a 195* and found nothing else wrong. Just told me when they pulled it in, thats the way it was, that it was total crap when I dropped it off. Had to buy a new 160* because the car woulndt run without it. Took it to a friends garage where we found all the other stuff and fixed it for about $1,000 total. Then they had nerve to call me and ask what I thought of their service......ha......I told them they were lucky I didnt sue them. Sorry so long a post, but I now hate dealerships with a passion for service.||||reg||1
Z||000015||DKOV||12-23-2001||12:52 PM||||The laid back service attendant at a FULL service fuel pump -<P>"Uh, M sorry to say but when'in I went to check yer earl, somebody done stole yer injun!"<P>You reply -<P>"It's in the back"<P>He replies -<P>"Nosir, we don't carry injuns"<P>You reply - <P>"No, the engine is IN the back of THIS car."<P>He replies -<P>"You college types... per-par'd for anythin'... carryin' a spare!  I aint putin' in in though, I tell you what!"<P>You reply -<P>"Thanks for the gas."<P>He replies -<P>"Few-whee! We sell some-em in the store fer that."<P>You reply - <P>"For what?"<P>He replies -<P>"Yer gas"<P>You reply - <P>"Not me, the car!"<P>He replies -<P>"Yer car has Gas?"<P>You reply -<P>"No, the car NEEDS gas!"<P>He replies - <P>"But you got gas."<P>You reply - <P>"Yes, I do... but"<P>He replies -<P>"Y'know, we got some-em in the store fer that"<P>You LEAVE<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>DKOV -<P>OK... I was bored.  But it COULD happen  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">||||reg||1
